    "description": "JFK New Terminal One is the public-private partnership developing and operating a new international terminal at John F. Kennedy International Airport in Queens, New York. Its customers are airlines and air passengers using one of the largest international gateway airports in the United States. The project follows an asset-heavy concession and terminal operating model supported by long-term aviation traffic and airline use rather than an asset-light services model. Public materials describe a 2.4 million-square-foot terminal and a total project cost of approximately $9.5 billion, making it one of the largest airport terminal redevelopments in North America. Swiss Life Asset Managers committed a minority equity stake in July 2022 alongside the existing consortium, and the project has since advanced through groundbreaking and multiple green bond financings.",
